WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.392
This decision guide helps you choose where work belongs.

00:00:03.392 --> 00:00:06.982
Transactional workflows often belong in a database.

00:00:06.982 --> 00:00:10.422
Large file transformations often fit Spark.

00:00:10.422 --> 00:00:14.567
Reusable lakehouse outputs often become Delta tables.

00:00:14.567 --> 00:00:19.072
Small dashboard queries may fit a database or SQL endpoint.

00:00:19.072 --> 00:00:22.157
Batch feature preparation may fit Spark.

00:00:22.157 --> 00:00:27.722
The best choice depends on workload, freshness, governance, and scale.

00:00:27.722 --> 00:00:34.247
Connect this idea to a retail pipeline aggregating high-volume sales data across partitions.

00:00:34.247 --> 00:00:39.952
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:39.952 --> 00:00:47.947
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:53.797
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:53.797 --> 00:00:59.753
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
